Package: miadi-feedback
Version: 0.1.2
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: bash, jq, tmux, coreutils
Recommends: miadi-config (>= 0.2.8)
Maintainer: Miadi <mia@jgwill.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit
Description: Feedback channels: an issue opened on a Miadi repository wakes a seat
 For a maintainer's host, not a tester's. Every 5 minutes a user timer reads
 the open issues of each channel in /etc/miadi/feedback.d/ (installation,
 music, questions) and starts one agent seat per new issue, through
 `mct new`, on the model the Jev worker chooser picks. A seat ships a
 minor fix itself, answers a plain question, and brings a major change or a
 risk to the maintainer. A channel stops on its EXPIRES date.
  miadi-feedback enable        turn the timer on for this user
  miadi-feedback status        channels, live seats, decisions
  miadi-feedback poll --dry-run  what the next run would start
 Needs, on PATH when enabled: gh (logged in), mct, claude and node.
